# With DevTools open in a Little Window, the Little Window still takes the window's actions: ⌥⌘I closes
# its DevTools, and the browser window's tab is left alone. Up to engine -17, Chrome's own (hidden) DevTools
# window became key when DevTools opened (key=none little=none after Inspect), so ⌥⌘I and the rest went to
# the browser window's tab instead: it opened DevTools there and the Little Window's stayed open.
budget rss=900 stalls50=40
seed settings.json {"hasSeenImportPrompt": true, "toolbarDefaultMigrated": true, "defaultLinkDestination": {"littleWindow": {}}}
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=main
expect-log loaded 127\.0\.0\.1 \(HTTP 200\)
cra://debug?externalURL=${PAGE}?n=little
wait 3
cra://debug?target=little&inspectAt=40,40
wait 5
cra://debug?devToolsShown=inspected
expect-log little devtools inspected: little0 peek=0 parked=0 open=1 docked=1 shown=1
cra://debug?front=inspected
# Nothing of Cra's is key when another app took the keyboard during the run; the Little Window in front
# still takes the actions then. Chrome's window key (the bug) gives little=none.
expect-log front inspected: key=(LittleWindow|none) little=little0

cra://action/devTools
wait 3
cra://debug?devToolsShown=closed
expect-log little devtools closed: little0 peek=0 parked=0 open=0 pageFills=1
expect-log tab devtools closed: windows=1 open=0
